WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:05.320
Game of Thrones Season 8 Episode 5 is The
Bells.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:09.309
It starts with Varys, writing letters about
Jon’s Targaryen identity.

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:13.530
He’s spreading the word and getting support
for Jon to be King.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.600
Varys speaks with Martha, one of his spies
or little birds.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:23.539
Apparently, she and Varys are trying to poison
Daenerys . So Varys is betraying Daenerys,

00:00:23.539 --> 00:00:25.730
and now supports Jon.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:30.369
Varys tells Jon that he would be a good king
, which might not be true.

00:00:30.369 --> 00:00:35.960
Jon is good at leading and fighting, but he
has no experience with southern politics – with

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:39.239
council meetings, plots and intrigue.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:43.809
Jon is a lot like his uncle Ned – an honourable
honest northman.

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:48.430
And Ned only lasted a season in the capital
before he was outplayed and killed.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:53.160
Jon only lasted as Commander of the Night’s
Watch for a season before he was killed.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:56.770
Meanwhile Daenerys has been learning to rule
for eight seasons.

00:00:56.770 --> 00:01:01.250
So why is Varys so sure that Jon would be
a better ruler?

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:06.550
Varys says “every time a Targaryen is born,
the gods toss a coin and the world holds its

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:10.750
breath” . It’s a common saying, because
while some Targaryen kings have been wise

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:16.640
and good, others have been violent and cruel,
like Dany’s father the Mad King.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:22.300
Varys is worried that Dany might snap and
burn King’s Landing . As it turns out, he’s

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:27.810
right, but up until now, Dany’s been very
reasonable in her conquest of Westeros.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:32.430
She tried all of Tyrion’s stupid plans to
end the war peacefully, and she came north

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:35.950
to save the world from white walkers, when
she could’ve just taken the Throne.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:41.000
She’s doing all the right things, so why
is Varys is so certain she’s nuts that he

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.340
tries to poison her?

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:47.940
Varys had once supported Viserys Targaryen,
but Daenerys is too crazy for him?

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:52.410
In the books, Varys has totally different
motivations, that make a lot more sense – go

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:54.030
watch that video.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:57.420
But here, he supports Jon over Daenerys.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:00.650
Jon says he’s loyal to Dany, that she’s
his queen.

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:07.210
But Varys says “Men decide where power resides”
. This refers to Varys’ riddle in Season

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:12.660
2 . The idea is that kings and priests and
money only have power if people believe they

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:13.920
have power.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:19.230
Jon sees power in Daenerys, but he could choose
to see power in himself.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:24.760
Tyrion finds out about Varys’ betrayal and
tells Daenerys . And Daenerys is unsurprised,

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:27.750
she’s numb to any more loss.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:33.100
She had begged Jon not to reveal his identity,
but he told Sansa, and Sansa told Tyrion,

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:38.680
to Varys, who used it to betray Daenerys . All
of her allies have failed her.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:41.760
Missandei Rhaegal and Jorah are dead.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.950
Dany feels there is no one she can trust – like
everyone’s against her, no matter what she

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:51.450
does .
Daenerys executes Varys, and he calmly accepts

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:52.480
his fate.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:56.000
He was willing to risk his life for the sake
of the realm.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:01.780
Tyrion tells Varys that he snitched on him
to Dany . Tyrion feels guilty for betraying

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:08.410
one of his only friends . They say farewell,
and Dany burns Varys alive, just as she promised

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:12.940
she would .
Daenerys and Grey Worm grieve for Missandei.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:18.180
Grey Worm throws her old slave collar into
fire – Missandei’s last word was dracarys,

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.180
which means dragonfire.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:24.970
So Dany and Grey Worm will express their grief
in fiery violence.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:30.620
Daenerys confronts Jon for telling Sansa about
his identity, even though she begged him not

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:31.620
to.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:34.540
Can Daenerys rely on her lover Jon?

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.840
She kisses him, but he pulls away.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:42.420
He was disturbed to see her burn Varys, so
Jon’s not too keen on macking his aunt.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:47.070
With even Jon rejecting her, Dany feels that
no one in Westeros loves her.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:52.900
She decides to use fear to take power .
Dany decides to attack King’s Landing.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:57.220
Tyrion warns that that would kill thousands
of innocents , but Dany says that’s worth

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:59.360
it if they can remove Cersei.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.450
And that’s not an unusual attitude in Westeros.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:05.440
When the lords make war, common folk die.

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:10.420
Like, twenty years ago, the Lannisters killed
many innocent people in King’s Landing removing

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:15.110
the Mad King . But Tyrion hopes for Daenerys
to take the capital peacefully – he says

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:19.880
if the city bells ring, that means they’ve
surrendered, so the attack can stop . Dany

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:24.110
agrees, but she’s clearly keen for fire
and blood.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:26.880
Arya and the Hound pass through the war camp.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.300
Arya says she’s going to kill Cersei.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:32.530
If she mentioned that earlier, Daenerys could
have held off the attack.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:38.070
There’d be no need for battle and no dead
civilians if Arya snuck in and killed Cersei

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:42.300
. But Arya’s too edgy and cool to share
her plans with Jon.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:47.390
Tyrion frees Jaime – he was captured by
Daenerys trying to get to Cersei . Tyrion

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:51.920
wants Jaime to convince Cersei to surrender
, so that the people of King’s Landing won’t

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:56.550
die . It’s funny that Tyrion is trying so
hard to save these people, when in Season

00:04:56.550 --> 00:05:01.310
4, he said wanted to kill the people of King’s
Landing . In the books, Tyrion’s still in

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:07.440
this dark, vengeful place, but in the show,
Daenerys has changed Tyrion’s worldview,

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:10.190
inspired him to believe in a better world.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:12.460
Jaime doesn’t believe in a better world.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:17.370
He says he never cared about the people of
King’s Landing – which is weird, because

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:22.570
Jaime once killed his king to save the people
of King’s Landing – to stop the Mad King

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:24.620
from burning the city.

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:28.590
Maybe this is just Jaime using his Kingslayer
persona again.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:33.470
He’s acting cruel and careless to hide how
conflicted he really is.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:38.410
Over the last eight seasons, Jaime’s grown
beyond that Kingslayer persona.

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:43.000
He left Cersei and risked his life to fight
for the living with Brienne.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:48.330
But now he’s suddenly regressing back to
the selfish person he used to be.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:53.290
Tyrion gets Davos to put a boat outside the
Red Keep so that Jaime and Cersei can escape

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:59.330
. Jaime once saved Tyrion’s life, so now
Tyrion tries to save his . The brothers have

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:02.490
a heartfelt farewell.

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:05.760
In the capital, Cersei prepares to defend
her Throne.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:10.320
She brings common people up around the Red
Keep – thinking that Daenerys won’t wanna

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:15.820
hurt innocent people . The Golden Company,
and Euron’s fleet are defending the city,

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:18.030
until Daenerys attacks.

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:24.010
She flies down from above, with the sun behind
her, and wipes out the entire Iron Fleet,

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:29.570
even though the Fleet has dozens of scorpion
ballistas . Last episode, Euron hit the dragon

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:32.160
Rhaegal with three scorpion bolts.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:36.680
Daenerys and Drogon couldn’t handle just
eleven of Euron’s ships.

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:41.889
This time, Euron has over a hundred ships,
and Daenerys destroys them all.

00:06:41.889 --> 00:06:48.160
She also burns the dozens of scorpions on
the city walls , and not one scorpion bolt

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:49.160
hits.

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:54.770
The scorpions went from a huge threat to a
non-issue in one episode.

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:57.070
The same thing happens with the Golden Company.

00:06:57.070 --> 00:07:02.070
Cersei went to a lot of trouble to hire these
guys, borrowing money from Iron Bank, having

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:04.180
Euron ship them cross the sea.

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:08.710
Cersei says they’re “the most powerful
army in Essos” . But Daenerys wipes them

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:10.660
out before they can do anything.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:14.830
Her soldiers attack, and quickly overwhelm
the Lannisters.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:19.470
So the show leads us to believe that we’ll
get a big epic battle between the good guys

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:20.470
and bad guys.

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:25.010
But the show subverts that by having Daenerys
easily stomp Cersei’s army.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:29.240
It leads us to question whether Dany and Jon
really are the good guys.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:35.389
A lot of these shots echo the Battle of the
Bastards, except now Jon is on the other side.

00:07:35.389 --> 00:07:37.759
And it gets worse from here.

00:07:37.759 --> 00:07:41.070
The Lannisters surrender, and the city bells
ring.

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.270
So Daenerys achieves the impossible.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:46.390
She takes the capital with very few deaths.

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:52.039
She can just go to the Red Keep, arrest Cersei,
end the war , so Dany can take the Throne

00:07:52.039 --> 00:07:56.850
as a peaceful queen, a liberator and protector
of the people.

00:07:56.850 --> 00:08:02.930
This is what Daenerys always wanted, but when
it happens, she doesn’t feel happy . She

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:08.810
only feels grief and anger . She’s lost
Missandei, and Rhaegal, and Jorah.

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:12.460
Everyone’s turned against her, despite all
her sacrifices.

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:19.040
She feels alone , and overwhelmed, and she
snaps . She burns the city and the innocent

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:20.449
people in it.

00:08:20.449 --> 00:08:25.100
She spends the rest of the episode systematically
destroying King’s Landing.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:30.710
By the end, most of the city is afire, and
there are a million people in there . So Daenerys

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:37.319
kills hundreds of thousands of innocent men
women and children, not for any strategic

00:08:37.319 --> 00:08:40.200
reason, but because she’s angry.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:45.140
And sure, maybe she’s inspiring fear to
force people to follow her . But it’s clear

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:50.329
from the scene, and from interviews with actors
and showrunners, that this isn’t a political

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:56.640
calculation, this is an emotional outburst
that leads to the deaths of hundreds of thousands

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:58.879
of innocent people.

00:08:58.879 --> 00:09:04.470
This is more death and destruction than anyone
has ever caused in Game of Thrones.

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:09.889
Tywin and Cersei and Ramsay never killed hundreds
of thousands of civilians.

00:09:09.889 --> 00:09:15.149
Only the white walkers are that bad – so
Daenerys is arguably as evil as the Night

00:09:15.149 --> 00:09:16.149
King.

00:09:16.149 --> 00:09:21.589
He brought an apocalypse of ice, now she brings
an apocalypse of fire – which nicely sums

00:09:21.589 --> 00:09:27.619
up the Robert Frost poem that inspired this
series – the world could end in ice or fire,

00:09:27.619 --> 00:09:33.059
either would suffice . So there is meaning
here – it’s about how human conflict is

00:09:33.059 --> 00:09:38.309
just as destructive as magic white walkers
– like, the humans defeated the zombies,

00:09:38.309 --> 00:09:41.500
but turns out that humans were real monsters
all along.

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:46.720
It’s kind of a cliché, but author George
Martin always said that Thrones isn’t about

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:52.060
good guys and bad guys , it’s about “the
human heart in conflict with itself” . Human

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:57.240
nature is what destroys King’s Landing,
so this disaster does fit with the themes

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:58.279
of the series.

00:09:58.279 --> 00:10:00.240
But how does it fit Dany’s character?

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:03.839
Is she really this evil?

00:10:03.839 --> 00:10:09.620
Daenerys has always struggled to balance violence
and vengeance against peace and compromise.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:14.819
She wants to be a fair ruler, but sometimes
she gets angry, and does violence that isn’t

00:10:14.819 --> 00:10:17.110
politically smart or just.

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:22.470
Like in Season 4, she crucified a hundred
Masters . In Season 5, she fed Masters to

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:27.490
her dragons, even though she said some might
be “innocent” . And in Season 7, she burned

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:28.689
the Tarlys.

00:10:28.689 --> 00:10:35.170
Some of these might be justifiable, but they
were killings motivated by anger, a Targaryen

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:37.769
urge for fire and blood.

00:10:37.769 --> 00:10:43.199
And Dany’s often wanted to go further, to
let her dragons loose and to burn all her

00:10:43.199 --> 00:10:44.199
enemies.

00:10:44.199 --> 00:10:49.120
In Season 2, she threatens Qarth, saying she’ll
“burn cities to the ground” . In Season

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:54.569
4, she decides to kill every Master in Yunkai
, and in Season 6, to kill the Meereenese,

00:10:54.569 --> 00:10:59.980
to “return their cities to the dirt” . Both
these times, Daenerys’ advisors convince

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:02.050
her not to wipe out cities.

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:07.749
Jorah and Tyrion “check her worst impulses”
. So in Season 8, when Jorah’s dead, and

00:11:07.749 --> 00:11:11.809
Dany’s lost faith in Tyrion, there’s no
one to hold her back.

00:11:11.809 --> 00:11:16.209
She expresses her grief and rage in fire and
blood.

00:11:16.209 --> 00:11:21.899
When Aegon the Conqueror’s sister died,
Aegon burned every castle and keep in Dorne

00:11:21.899 --> 00:11:27.249
, the civilian deaths were “uncountable”
. This is what Targaryens do, this is what

00:11:27.249 --> 00:11:30.760
dragons represent – destruction, fire, fury.

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:35.500
But why would Daenerys attack civilians?

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:40.110
Part of what defines her as a character is
her sympathy for the common people, for the

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:41.680
weak and innocent.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:45.939
Cause as a child, Daenerys herself was treated
as a slave.

00:11:45.939 --> 00:11:50.059
Abused by her brother, sold to Drogo, used
and raped.

00:11:50.059 --> 00:11:54.360
So as soon as she starts getting power, she
uses it to protect the vulnerable.

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:57.519
She saves Lhazarene women, she protects her
khalasar.

00:11:57.519 --> 00:12:00.120
She spends three seasons liberating slaves.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:04.619
Daenerys once locked away her dragons to prevent
them from hurting kids.

00:12:04.619 --> 00:12:11.259
So, angry or not, murdering hundreds of thousands
of innocents goes against one of the foundations

00:12:11.259 --> 00:12:13.259
of Daenerys’ character.

00:12:13.259 --> 00:12:17.910
If this happens in the books, we might see
a more gradual progression into this violence,

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:20.730
so we can better understand why she does this.

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:25.009
Or the situation could be different, like
maybe Dany will only kill the people at the

00:12:25.009 --> 00:12:28.529
Red Keep, who are in the way of the Throne.

00:12:28.529 --> 00:12:33.769
Or she could will accidentally burn the city,
by setting off this wildfire – the wildfire’s

00:12:33.769 --> 00:12:38.269
left over from when the Mad King tried to
burn the city, so Daenerys is unknowingly

00:12:38.269 --> 00:12:41.549
ignites her father’s legacy.

00:12:41.549 --> 00:12:46.470
Whatever her reasons, Daenerys has become
what she came to destroy – she’s queen

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:51.239
of the ashes, a bringer of death, a tyrant.

00:12:51.239 --> 00:12:55.999
Grey Worm sparks violence on the ground, attacking
the Lannisters who’d surrendered, to avenge

00:12:55.999 --> 00:12:58.170
the death of Missandei.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:12:59.910
And the Stark soldiers join in.

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:04.269
They also have reason to hate the Lannisters
– Lannisters killed their beloved Ned and

00:13:04.269 --> 00:13:08.450
King Robb, and gave the North to the brutal
Boltons.

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:13.290
Thousands of northmen died in wars against
the Lannisters, so now they get revenge.

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:18.079
It’s a bit like in the books, when northmen
march against the Boltons, and a northman

00:13:18.079 --> 00:13:23.410
called Big Bucket Wull says “Let me bathe
in Bolton blood before I die”.

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:28.470
There’s a tradition in the north for older
northmen to get themselves killed before winter,

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:32.980
so that their families have one less mouth
to feed . Many the northmen who came south

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:35.799
with Jon might not be planning to return.

00:13:35.799 --> 00:13:39.420
So it’s no surprise that this becomes a
bloodbath.

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:44.339
Jon watches in horror as his men slaughter
and rape civilians.

00:13:44.339 --> 00:13:49.100
In Season 3, Jorah says “There's a beast
in every man, and it stirs when you put a

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:53.379
sword in his hand” . We like to think of
the northmen as good guys.

00:13:53.379 --> 00:13:59.449
But the story shows how even people with good
intentions can become monsters in war .

00:13:59.449 --> 00:14:03.600
Arya and the Hound reach the Keep, and the
Hound tells her to turn back.

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:07.249
Arya wants to kill Cersei and finish her death
list.

00:14:07.249 --> 00:14:10.829
But the Hound tells her not to become like
him.

00:14:10.829 --> 00:14:15.939
The Hound’s been obsessed with revenge all
his life – ever since his brother the Mountain

00:14:15.939 --> 00:14:17.459
burned his face.

00:14:17.459 --> 00:14:22.939
That anger and bitterness is why the Hound
is so lonely, cynical and unhappy.

00:14:22.939 --> 00:14:28.209
If Arya kills Cersei, it’ll only take her
deeper into violence and alienation.

00:14:28.209 --> 00:14:34.170
The Hound says if she stays here, she’ll
die – she could die literally from the collapsing

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:39.100
castle, but she could also die metaphorically,
if her humanity is consumed by violence and

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:43.009
hate – like how Meera said that Bran “died”.

00:14:43.009 --> 00:14:47.190
So Arya chooses life, and turns back from
the precipice.

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:52.319
She thanks the Hound, and calls him Sandor,
his real name . It’s a final moment of human

00:14:52.319 --> 00:14:55.939
connection between Arya and Sandor Clegane.

00:14:55.939 --> 00:14:59.709
So Arya turns back, but the Hound thinks it’s
too late for him.

00:14:59.709 --> 00:15:01.749
He goes and finds his brother.

00:15:01.749 --> 00:15:05.980
[tasteful airhorns] These two have wanted
to kill each other for years, and here at

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:08.990
the end of the world seems as good a time
as any.

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:13.939
Qyburn orders the Mountain to stay, but he
disobeys, and kills his creator.

00:15:13.939 --> 00:15:19.040
Remember, the Mountain had been all but dead
when Qyburn raised him as a zombie man with

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:21.809
some mix of science and necromancy.

00:15:21.809 --> 00:15:27.730
Qyburn is like Dr Frankenstein, and the Mountain
is his monster, so it’s neatly poetic for

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:30.649
Qyburn to be killed by his creation.

00:15:30.649 --> 00:15:34.949
We see the Mountain’s face is all rotted,
and no matter what the Hound does to him,

00:15:34.949 --> 00:15:36.290
he won’t die.

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:41.949
Cause Gregor is already dead – the brother
who burned Sandor is long gone, all that’s

00:15:41.949 --> 00:15:44.169
left is a walking corpse.

00:15:44.169 --> 00:15:47.749
This shows the pointlessness of and emptiness
of revenge.

00:15:47.749 --> 00:15:50.860
The Hound will never find happiness by killing
a dead man.

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:56.019
But the Hound feels this can only end with
death, so he takes the Mountain down with

00:15:56.019 --> 00:16:00.379
him, pushing him through a wall into the fires
below.

00:16:00.379 --> 00:16:05.259
Fire is what started their beef when Gregor
burned Sandor – and fire is only thing that

00:16:05.259 --> 00:16:07.299
could kill the undead Mountain.

00:16:07.299 --> 00:16:10.079
So the brothers burn together.

00:16:10.079 --> 00:16:15.759
Jaime tries to reach Cersei by a passage to
the Red Keep, but he’s stopped by Euron.

00:16:15.759 --> 00:16:21.079
Euron survived Dany’s attack on his fleet,
and he rises from the sea – the ironborn

00:16:21.079 --> 00:16:26.189
have a ritual of drowning themselves then
being revived – “What is dead may never

00:16:26.189 --> 00:16:32.199
die”, “But rises again, harder and stronger”
. Euron starts a fight with Jaime – they’ve

00:16:32.199 --> 00:16:35.419
been rivals for Cersei’s love since last
season.

00:16:35.419 --> 00:16:40.290
Jaime kills Euron, but Jaime’s badly wounded,
so Euron’s happy that he’s the man who

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:46.369
killed Jaime Lannister . Euron in the show
is a simple man with simple goals.

00:16:46.369 --> 00:16:51.160
He wanted to be a king, to fuck the queen,
and to kill Jaime – and with that done,

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:53.209
he dies content.

00:16:53.209 --> 00:16:58.540
Jaime gets to Cersei, and the twins embrace
as the world falls down around them.

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:01.739
They try to escape, but their passage is blocked
by rubble.

00:17:01.739 --> 00:17:08.110
Cersei had stayed defiant while Daenerys burned
the city, but now she breaks down and cries

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:13.250
for the life of her baby and herself, cause
deep down, Cersei’s only human.

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:17.740
Jaime tells her that she and him are the only
things that matter in the world , just as

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:19.860
they said in Season 1.

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:22.959
And then the roof collapses and they die.

00:17:22.959 --> 00:17:25.220
This is a poetic end for Cersei.

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:30.670
She’s crushed beneath the Red Keep, the
symbol of the power that she wanted so badly

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:32.540
that it destroyed her.

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:36.550
Cersei could have saved herself at any time
in the last couple seasons.

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:41.970
But Cersei couldn’t let go of power, and
so it collapsed upon her.

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:46.630
Cersei’s pregnancy plotline went nowhere
– all that stuff about whether Jaime or

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:51.420
Euron was the father, and whether the baby
would make Cersei cooperative…

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:55.970
Maybe the showrunners thought that a baby
would humanise Cersei, as though the motherhood

00:17:55.970 --> 00:18:00.580
is the only relatable aspect of Cersei’s
deep complex character.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:06.990
In the last two seasons, Cersei did very little
but get pregnant drink wine and die.

00:18:06.990 --> 00:18:09.880
Jaime’s death makes him a failure.

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:14.920
He tried to redeem himself, and to be a better
man, with Brienne, but he couldn’t escape

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:16.870
Cersei, and dies with her.

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:21.780
Jaime changes so much throughout his arc,
but he ends up dying in the same place he

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:24.880
began . Maybe this is realistic.

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:26.730
Some people don’t change.

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:31.990
The showrunners say Jaime’s love for Cersei
is like an addiction , and sometimes addicts

00:18:31.990 --> 00:18:33.310
relapse, and overdose.

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:38.280
But you’ve gotta ask, what’s the point
of the last eight seasons of Jaime’s arc

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:41.560
if he abandons all his growth to die with
Cersei?

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:46.750
Jaime dies with his hand on Cersei’s neck,
which evokes the valonqar prophecy from the

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:52.310
books, which hints that Cersei will be strangled
to death by Jaime . It may be that in the

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:55.260
books, Jaime will kill Cersei before he dies.

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:59.620
That way, Jaime could overcome his darker
half before his death.

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:04.830
In Season 5, Jaime said he wants to die “In
the arms of the woman” he loves . Some fans

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:09.090
hoped that that would be Brienne, but – turns
out it was Cersei.

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:14.150
The prophecy of Maggy the Frog said that Cersei
would be cast down by someone “younger”

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:18.860
and “more beautiful” . Cersei thought
that meant Margaery – but turns out, it’s

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:21.730
Daenerys, bringing the Keep down onto Cersei.

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:26.760
Also, Daenerys could fit the Dothraki prophecy
of the “The stallion who mounts the world”,

00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:33.210
and tramples nations in to dust . So Season
8 does fulfil some of the series’ prophecies

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:35.320
and foreshadowing.

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:39.540
While the city burns, Arya sees the devastation
on the ground.

00:19:39.540 --> 00:19:42.240
She trained for seasons to be a servant of
death.

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:47.860
But now she sees how horrible death can be
– with hundreds of innocents suffering and

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:50.070
screaming and grieving.

00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:54.180
A common woman helps Arya – a moment of
hope in the darkness.

00:19:54.180 --> 00:19:58.920
So Arya tries to save the woman and other
civilians – they just end up dying anyway,

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:03.780
but the point is that Arya is trying to help
people instead of just killing for once.

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:09.330
After the devastation, Arya rises from the
ashes, and cries over the bodies of the people

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:11.150
she tried to save.

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:15.600
The visuals evoke Pompeii, and 9/11, and the
bombing of Dresden.

00:20:15.600 --> 00:20:22.380
Ash rains down like nuclear winter – author
George Martin says his dragons are like nukes

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:27.720
. Arya sees a horse – the only other living
creature among the death.

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:32.800
The horse is white with red blood, just like
a weirwood is white with red sap.

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:37.760
So this could connect to the old gods – some
fans think this horse was sent by Bran with

00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:39.520
his warging powers.

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:45.000
Or it could connect to the Book of Revelations,
in the Bible, where a pale horse means death.

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:49.380
But Arya strokes the horse, we hear its breathing
and see its face.

00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:55.200
Arya rides it out of the ruins, away from
the death and destruction – Arya and her

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:57.050
horse represent life.

00:20:57.050 --> 00:21:01.780
But overall, this is a very dark episode.

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:05.570
Hundreds of thousands are killed by the woman
we thought was a hero.

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:10.390
Jaime fails to become a better man, and dies
with his hateful sister.

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:16.180
All of Jon’s heroism, and Varys’ scheming,
and Tyrion’s supposed intelligence did nothing

00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:18.370
to prevent disaster.

00:21:18.370 --> 00:21:22.160
Is Game of Thrones really this bleak and nihilistic?

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:27.220
Thrones author George Martin says his “worldview
is anything but nihilistic” . Thrones is

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:32.330
full of death and darkness, but the darkness
is there to better show the light of human

00:21:32.330 --> 00:21:34.620
struggles against darkness.

00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:40.550
“Men’s lives have meaning, not their deaths”
. And yet this episode has little but death.

00:21:40.550 --> 00:21:43.230
There’s a sense of inevitability.

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:48.970
Varys talks about Targaryen madness, as though
Daenerys was destined to repeat her father’s

00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:49.970
sins.

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:55.090
Jaime just accepts that he could never be
better than the hateful man he was.

00:21:55.090 --> 00:21:58.250
The Hound basically commits suicide by Mountain.

00:21:58.250 --> 00:22:03.000
It’s as though all these character’s hopes
and growth were for nothing.

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:06.490
The dream of a better world is ash.

00:22:06.490 --> 00:22:11.060
What was the point of this story if it ends
with just failure and death?

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:15.630
The Thrones books always have some sense of
meaning against the darkness.

00:22:15.630 --> 00:22:19.910
Their ending will be bittersweet, not just
bitter.

00:22:19.910 --> 00:22:25.560
If Thrones is to be true to its source material,
and to rise above empty nihilism, it needs

00:22:25.560 --> 00:22:29.960
to show some hope in the series finale next
week.

00:22:29.960 --> 00:22:35.710
There are many great Game of Thrones YouTube
channels, and a bunch of them just wrote a

00:22:35.710 --> 00:22:41.490
